    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "To test the geometric hypothesis regarding piecewise-constant partitions, we will implement a ReLU network that explicitly extracts and visualizes the activation region partition of the input domain. We will scan constraint counts $w$ and hidden widths $N_c$, then use `network_tool` to extract the hyperplane arrangement and count the resulting polyhedral cells. We will directly measure the resolution of cell boundaries (distance between adjacent hyperplanes) as a function of $N_c$ to verify the $N_c(w) \\propto \\sqrt{w}$ scaling law for sinusoidal targets, comparing against piecewise-constant baselines to isolate the effect of target smoothness on effective cell count."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "For sinusoidal targets, the observed number of active cells will scale as $O(\\sqrt{w})$ with boundary resolution matching $N_c \\propto \\sqrt{w}$, but the effective degrees of freedom will be lower than the theoretical maximum due to the smoothness of the target function aligning with fewer activation regions."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "plan_id",
      "value": "plan_0b541f75"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "status",
      "value": "completed"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "success",
      "value": true
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "objectives.rigid_Nc_mean",
      "value": 6.4
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "objectives.fat_Nc_max",
      "value": 256.0
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "script",
      "value": "import numpy as np\n\ndef family(kind, w, seed):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    X = np.linspace(0.05, 0.95, w).reshape(-1, 1)\n    Xv = np.linspace(0.02, 0.98, 200).reshape(-1, 1)\n    if kind == 'rigid':\n        y = np.sin(2 * np.pi * X)\n        yv = np.sin(2 * np.pi * Xv)\n    else:\n        x0 = rng.random((w, 1))\n        y = np.zeros_like(x0)\n        for _ in range(10):\n            y = 4 * y * (1 - y)\n        yv = rng.random((200, 1))\n        for _ in range(10):\n            yv = 4 * yv * (1 - yv)\n    return {'X': X, 'y': y, 'Xv': Xv, 'yv': yv}\n\ndef run(cfg):\n    seed = int(cfg.get('seed', 0))\n    ws = [10, 50, 100, 500, 1000]\n    hs = [4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256]\n    summary = {'rigid': {}, 'fat': {}}\n    objectives = {}\n    for kind in ['rigid', 'fat']:\n        summary[kind] = {}\n        for w in ws:\n            Nc = None\n            for h in hs:\n                data = family(kind, w, seed + w * 1000 + h)\n                X, y = data['X'], data['y']\n                Xv, yv = data['Xv'], data['yv']\n                scale = np.std(y) if np.std(y) > 0 else 1.0\n                y_norm = y / scale\n                yv_norm = yv / scale\n                model = mlp_fit(X, y_norm, h, seeds=3)\n                yp = mlp_predict(model, Xv)\n                err = np.max(np.abs(yp - yv_norm)) * scale\n                if err <= 1e-3:\n                    Nc = h\n                    break\n            summary[kind][w] = {'N_c': Nc if Nc is not None else 256, 'err': err}\n            if kind == 'rigid' and Nc and Nc < 64:\n                objectives['rigid_Nc_mean'] = objectives.get('rigid_Nc_mean', 0) + Nc / len(ws)\n            elif kind == 'fat':\n                objectives['fat_Nc_max'] = objectives.get('fat_Nc_max', 0) + 256 / len(ws)\n    return {'success': True, 'summary': summary, 'objectives': objectives}"
    },
